    {
      "id": 90,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        880
      ],
      "size": [
        430,
        1180
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Create Relief Image\n\nFour stages. **Every stage reads a FILE**, so an approved image is frozen on disk and cannot drift.\n\n## The one node that matters\n**Load Image** (teal, left) feeds BOTH Stage 1.5 and Stage 2. Whichever file you point it at is your position in the chain. There is no rewiring.\n\n## STAGE 1 - generate candidates  (blue, active)\n1. Run. Inspect the preview. Run again for another (seed is on `randomize`).\n2. Like one? Name it in **Save STAGE 1**'s `filename_prefix`, select that node, **Ctrl+M**, **Run**, then **Ctrl+M** back off.\n\n### Do NOT use the fixed-seed trick\n`control_after_generate: randomize` rolls the seed **after** each run, so the value in the widget is the *next* seed, not the one that made the image you are looking at. Switching to `fixed` locks the wrong seed. Save the file instead. (A seed is always recoverable from the PNG metadata.)\n\n## STAGE 1.5 - cleanup  (orange, muted)  --  OPTIONAL\nThis is defect repair, not general refinement. Use it when Stage 1 gave you a good bird with a bad presentation: a cast shadow, a ground plane, a busy or uneven background, anything behind the bird. Those are the defects that break the segmentation later.\n\n3. Copy your Stage 1 file into `ComfyUI/input` and pick it in **Load Image**.\n4. Orange **STAGE 1.5** title bar -> **Ctrl+M** -> **Run**. Inspect, and save it if it is better.\n\n**Skip this stage** if Stage 1 was already clean. Two img2img passes drift further from the image you approved than one, and Stage 2 is itself an img2img pass.\n\n## STAGE 2 - convert to carved relief  (magenta, muted)\n5. Point **Load Image** at whichever file you are happy with - the Stage 1 file, or the cleaned Stage 1.5 file.\n6. Magenta title bar -> **Ctrl+M** -> **Run**.\n7. You want: matte, chisel-cut planes, hard shadows inside the grooves, flat background, **no shine**, pose unchanged. Save it.\n\n## STAGE 3 - depth map  (green, muted)\n8. Green title bar -> **Ctrl+M** -> **Run**. Reads Stage 2's live output.\n9. Near surfaces bright, far dark. Beak and breast brightest, tail darkest.\n\n## Prompting Klein - the one rule\nKlein runs at **CFG 1.0**, where the negative branch is mathematically inert. `no shadow` or `no branch` subtracts nothing - the encoder just receives the concept. **Phrase every constraint as something to draw, never something to avoid.** Avoid left/right too: it is ambiguous and the model may render both interpretations, which is what produced the two-raven images. Use frame-relative wording: \"beak pointing toward the right edge\".\n\n## Depth resolution ladder\n`DA3Inference resolution` = **1428**, must be a multiple of 14. Attention cost grows with the square of token count, so on 8 GB: **1008** safe, **1428** current, **2016** may OOM. Step down if it fails.\n\n## Saving\nNothing auto-saves. All four **Save Image** nodes are parked outside the groups, so unmuting a stage never turns saving on. Name files `subject_pose_variant`."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
